.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (20, 5)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Customer ID</th><th>Customer Name</th><th>Region Name</th><th>Segment</th><th>Sales In Dollars</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>i32</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>740150</td><td>&quot;Barton LLC&quot;</td><td>&quot;US&quot;</td><td>&quot;Gold&quot;</td><td>215000</td></tr><tr><td>714466</td><td>&quot;Trantow-Barrows&quot;</td><td>&quot;EMEA&quot;</td><td>&quot;Silver&quot;</td><td>430000</td></tr><tr><td>218895</td><td>&quot;Kulas Inc&quot;</td><td>&quot;EMEA&quot;</td><td>&quot;Platinum&quot;</td><td>410000</td></tr><tr><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td></tr><tr><td>257198</td><td>&quot;Cronin, Oberbrunner and Spence…</td><td>&quot;US&quot;</td><td>&quot;Platinum&quot;</td><td>425000</td></tr><tr><td>604255</td><td>&quot;Halvorson, Crona and Champlin&quot;</td><td>&quot;US&quot;</td><td>null</td><td>430000</td></tr><tr><td>163416</td><td>&quot;Purdy-Kunde&quot;</td><td>&quot;APAC&quot;</td><td>&quot;Silver&quot;</td><td>410000</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


<br>
The only column without a space in the dataframe above is `Segment`. I can access this column using the dot method as shown below.

::: {#b38a0aad .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
df.select(pl.col.Segment)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (20, 1)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Segment</th></tr><tr><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Gold&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Silver&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Platinum&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&hellip;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Platinum&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Silver&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


<br>
However, I cannot use the dot method to access any of the columns with spaces, for instance, `Customer ID`. To access it I need to enclose the column name in square quotation marks as shown below.

::: {#49b37f75 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
df.select(pl.col('Customer ID'))
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}
```{=html}
